## Skill Router

Skills are expected under `~/.cursor/skills/` (or project `.cursor/skills/`). Some are authored in this catalog; others are vendored from [superpowers](https://github.com/obra/superpowers) or [SkillSpector](https://github.com/NVIDIA/SkillSpector) into the same directory, with no distinction at call time.

| Trigger | Skill | Notes |
|---------|-------|-------|
| Commit / "commit this" | `commit` | User-invoked (`/commit`) — hybrid message format |
| Pin domain language, glossary, architectural decision, or architecture fork | `grill-me` | **Default** for forks — one question at a time; updates `CONTEXT.md` / ADRs |
| Front/back or service-to-service boundary that must not drift: OpenAPI, AsyncAPI, JSON Schema, generated types | `contract-first` | Adapted from ECC (MIT) |
| End session / hand work to another agent | `handoff` | User-invoked; save to `context/handoffs/` |
| Terse / token-efficient replies | `caveman` | Levels: lite, full, ultra, wenyan-* (default on via rule) |
| Document a resolved env/tooling fix | `less-trouble` | Writes `docs/troubleshoot/TROUBLESHOOT.md` |
| Reverse-engineer legacy / undocumented code | `teach-me` | Cited docs under `context/rg/` |
| Curated workspace map before broad exploration | `map-architecture` | Maintains `context/architecture-graph.json` |
| Initialise / standardise repo docs | `init-repo` | User-invoked (`/init-repo`) |
| Asked whether a skill or skill folder is safe to install | `skill-inspector` | Vendored SkillSpector; static scan needs `skillspector` CLI when available |
| Any bug, test failure, unexpected behavior | `systematic-debugging` | Root cause before fixes; symptom fixes are failure |
| Feature or fix with tests first | `test-driven-development` | Red → green → refactor; watch the test fail |
| Create or improve a skill | `writing-skills` | Skill authoring as TDD on process docs |
| Turn an idea into a design, before implementing | `brainstorming` | Design dialogue — not a substitute for `grill-me` on forks; save to `context/specs/` |
| Write, then run, an implementation plan | `writing-plans`, `executing-plans`, `subagent-driven-development` | Save to app `context/plans/`; inline vs one subagent per task |
| Ask for or respond to a code review | `requesting-code-review`, `receiving-code-review` | Verify before implementing feedback |
| About to claim work is done | `verification-before-completion` | Evidence before assertions |
| Isolation, parallel work, closing a branch | `using-git-worktrees`, `dispatching-parallel-agents`, `finishing-a-development-branch` | |

If a task fits a skill above, load and follow that skill. Do not reinvent its process inline.

**`grill-me` vs `brainstorming`:** an architecture fork with real trade-offs goes to `grill-me` — one question at a time, and the outcome lands in `CONTEXT.md` or an ADR. Open-ended feature shaping goes to `brainstorming`, which produces a design document under `context/specs/`. When both fit, `grill-me` wins; `architecture-forks.mdc` makes that non-optional.

